#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:4
msgid ""
"Analyze the current project and populate the Hero knowledge base with "
"initial entries plus code intelligence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:6
msgid "Load the `project-context-generation` skill for enrichment guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:8
msgid "Run `hero scan --dry-run` first to preview what will be detected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:9
msgid ""
"Review the output with the user — check that languages, frameworks, and "
"tools are correctly identified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:10
msgid ""
"If the preview looks good, run `hero scan` to generate entries and code "
"intelligence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:11
msgid ""
"Enrich only the **stub knowledge entries** that are short and clearly "
"placeholders. **Do not rewrite code-intelligence files** (anything under "
"`.hero/knowledge/code/` — those are regenerated on every scan). Cap "
"enrichment to at most the five highest-value entries: any generated "
"overview / stack / project-structure / conventions / decisions stubs. "
"Apply the `project-context-generation` skill's guidance, then **stop** — "
"report what you changed and what you intentionally left alone, and end "
"the workflow. Do not chase tangents about glob configs, local dev "
"tooling, or AGENTS.md formatting unless the user asks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:13
msgid ""
"The scan automatically includes code intelligence (packages, symbols, "
"dependencies, hot files) unless `code_scan.depth` is set to "
"`\"disabled\"` in hero.json. Use `hero scan --code` to run only the code "
"intelligence scan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:15
msgid ""
"Use `--force` to overwrite existing entries when re-scanning after stack "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/scan.md:17
msgid "$ARGUMENTS"
msgstr ""

